window.EN={"1":"Prince Leif, this way.","2":"Father August!? Why are you here?","3":"I had been devising a plan to rescue you, Prince, but it seems that is no longer necessary.","4":"...You seem to have been through a great deal, but I am glad you are safe above all.","5":"August, I have never hated the Empire as much as I do now.","6":"It took my parents, and now it has taken someone precious, someone I could call a mother...","7":"I hate the Empire... and I hate Raydrik, who commits every atrocity as its pawn!!","8":"Tell me, August. What must I do to fight them?","9":"If I can get her back, I'll do anything.","10":"Tell me, August!","11":"I am told Lady Eyvel was turned to stone by petrification magic.","12":"If that is true, I must ask you to give her up.","13":"! ...What do you mean!? Are you saying there's no way to turn her back!?","14":"No. With the holy staff called Kia, petrification can be undone.","15":"However, that staff was sealed by Manfroy, Archbishop of Loptr,","16":"and it is said that only those of his bloodline can use it.","17":"Manfroy's bloodline... No...","18":"This is a rumor, but deep beneath the Yied Desert there is a secret temple of Loptr,","19":"and they say the stone statues of many warriors are displayed there.","20":"Among them, I hear, are the young warriors captured in the Battle of Belhalla over a decade ago...","21":"Lady Eyvel's statue too will no doubt be placed in that temple in time.","22":"No... How can something so absurd be allowed!","23":"Your anger is entirely justified, but at present, all over this world, the \"absurd things\" you speak of are happening.","24":"Even on this Thracian peninsula, already thousands...","25":"no, tens of thousands of children have been captured and sent to the imperial capital, Belhalla.","26":"Especially here in Munster, where Loptr's power is strong, and in your homeland of Leonster, it is nearly every last one...","27":"One no longer sees children in the streets.","28":"Are the parents fine with having their children taken!? Why don't they fight for themselves!?","29":"Of course the citizens are fighting. It is so in Munster as well; resistance is occurring everywhere.","30":"But in the end they are unarmed citizens; they cannot hope to match the imperial army and the Loptr Church.","31":"Killed on the spot, or captured and executed... it is a pitiful thing.","32":"In particular, the methods of Loptr's mage corps, the \"Berg Rosen,\" are cruelty itself.","33":"If even one person resists, they burn every resident of that village at the stake or bury them alive. It is the very \"Dark Age\" of legend...","34":"The people have lost even the will to resist, and are in a state like slaves.","35":"It's that bad...","36":"Yes. Northern Thracia once had blue skies and was rich in green,","37":"but now it is covered by dark clouds that never clear...","38":"Prince, I understand that you are anxious about Lady Eyvel,","39":"but you surely have a more important mission.","40":"What is needed most in northern Thracia now","41":"is a hero who can draw out the strength of the people of northern Thracia and bind them together as a group that fights.","42":"...Whether he excels in valor or strategy is not the issue. It is the \"hero\" as an illusion.","43":"You, Prince, as the child of the tragic heroes Quan and Ethlyn, have that qualification by birth.","44":"Do you understand? If you rise up, the anti-imperial forces of northern Thracia will unite as one,","45":"and as a result, it may be possible to drive out the forces of the Empire and Loptr.","46":"I haven't given up on Eyvel, but I understand what you're saying, August.","47":"If you tell me to become the banner of northern Thracia's liberation, that's just what I want.","48":"To restore the Kingdom of Leonster, lead its army, and defeat the imperial forces...","49":"That is the dream Finn and I have always talked about together!","50":"If you'll assist me as my strategist, August, I won't shrink from any hardship!","51":"But can it really be done?","52":"Understood. Hearing that resolve is all I needed.","53":"For now, please think only of escaping.","54":"Many soldiers have sortied in pursuit of us. Is there a safe route?","55":"I believe it would be best to flee through the east service gate... But the problem is when you enter the castle town.","56":"If the lookouts spot you, it will summon a large enemy force, and escape will become difficult.","57":"Without being spotted by the lookouts? Is such a thing possible...","58":"We just have to stay out of the town, right? Then leave it to me.","59":"One at a time, I can put you on my Hermes and carry you.","60":"From the sky we can go over the walls, and there's no worry about the enemy spotting us.","61":"I see. Then we can escape without fighting. But will you two be all right?","62":"Hermes says he'll do his best for me.","63":"The truth is, pegasi only open their hearts to girls. They don't even like being touched by men.","64":"But Hermes says he'll put up with it... He's a boy, so he's good at enduring.","65":"...As for the escape, that will do.","66":"What remains is whether or not to visit the castle town... That is the question.","67":"Hey, you all right?","68":"I've heard the story. Hurry and get out of here.","69":"In a little while, Lord Ced and the others should come to help. Then things'll get a bit easier.","70":"Father, my apologies. It seems I've pushed extra baggage on you.","71":"Galzus, I believe you said. You are employed by Lord Raydrik, are you not?","72":"Why this girl... Is she someone connected to you?","73":"No... It's not like that, but...","74":"...Very well. She's rather large baggage for a man traveling alone, but I will look after her for a while.","75":"Well then, Sir Galzus, fortune in battle!","76":"I didn't notice... To think it was you...","77":"Good. Prince Leif seems to be safe still.","78":"Yes. It seems we made it in time somehow.","79":"Then from here, we will act as decoys and aid the prince's escape.","80":"I'm sorry to ask this of everyone, but we cannot let him die. Lend me your help.","81":"Yes, Lord Ced!","82":"We're about at our limit...","83":"We're moving to retreat now. Everyone withdraw before the enemy's main force arrives. Hurry!","84":"Ohh, swordsman Galzus, you're late!","85":"Do you want something with me?","86":"You can see for yourself. Prisoners have escaped. They're quite formidable. Lend me your strength!","87":"Heh, trifling...","88":"My little brother Boy was taken to a safe village by the people of the Magi Squad.","89":"Thank you so very much. I'll never forget this kindness as long as I live.","90":"It's not much by way of thanks, but I'll give you this secret book handed down in my family.","91":"It's said to be a book that bestows mysterious power. I wonder if it will be of use...","92":"I've already given up on Boy. No, it's all right. I don't hold a grudge against you...","93":"Hey, I've been waiting. Thanks for rescuing my sister Leena!","94":"Yeah, I know, I know. Here, take this!","95":"I don't really get it, but it turned up at the roots of the tree in the back garden.","96":"I think it's a page from some book. Looks like it has a story behind it, right?","97":"Maybe something good'll happen if you hold onto it. Not that I'd know!","98":"Tch, some liberation army. My sister Leena is still a prisoner!","99":"Don't you people act cool, when you can't do a thing!","100":"You are the ones who saved my daughter Emily, aren't you?","101":"Ahh, how can I ever thank you?","102":"This is our family heirloom, a Knight's Crest. I'm sure it will be of use.","103":"Ahh, Emily... where have you gone...","104":"Ohh, it's you people. I've been waiting.","105":"I hear you rescued my son Murphy.","106":"Thanks to you, I was able to hide him somewhere safe. Along with the other children, of course.","107":"I'm Hicks, an axe knight of Munster.","108":"I'm thoroughly fed up with that bastard Raydrik.","109":"I'll fight alongside you too. Glad to be with you!","110":"Go away! I've no business with you!","111":"Some liberation army. Some prince of Leonster.","112":"Don't talk big when you can't even save a single child.","113":"I hear you saved my little sister Bella. Thank you.","114":"We're poor, so we can't give you much of a reward,","115":"but if you like, please take this holy water.","116":"Bella... isn't coming back... Never mind... I won't expect anything from you...","117":"So you're the ones who rescued my grandson Cliff.","118":"Mm, just what I'd expect from companions of the hero Ced. I'm grateful.","119":"Oh, that's right, I forgot. I'll give you this rapier.","120":"No, no need to hold back. It's just a token of my feelings.","121":"Well, it can't be helped... Cliff isn't coming back, but one can't ask much of you, who aren't even crusaders.","122":"So the sun rises from the east after all...","123":"Lord Raydrik, it appears Prince Leif has escaped outside the castle.","124":"You fools, what are you doing!? Can't you catch one small fry like that!?","125":"Sir! My apologies!","126":"Have General Eisenau lead the knights in pursuit at once!","127":"If he flees into Thracian territory, it will become troublesome.","128":"Sir. Understood.","129":"By the way, what happened to that girl, Mareeta? I don't see her...","130":"...I had intended to report it later, but... the guard was attacked by someone, and the girl was taken...","131":"My apologies!","132":"Grr, useless, every last one of you!","133":"Do you not even have a guess as to whose doing it was!?","134":"There is no doubt they are highly skilled.","135":"Someone saw that bodyguard, Galzus, near the scene. Can he be trusted?","136":"Hmm... Galzus...","137":"There are those who say they saw the Brand of Od on that man's back.","138":"If that is true, he would be Isaachian royalty...","139":"Heh. I am not such a fool as to hire a bodyguard without checking his background.","140":"He is indeed Isaachian royalty.","141":"He is a prince of the fallen royal house of Ribaut, and since their parents were siblings, he is cousin to Prince Shannan of Isaach.","142":"Prince Shannan is one of the leaders of the anti-imperial forces, is he not?","143":"Is it not dangerous to keep a relative of such a man inside the castle?","144":"Heh. Do you know nothing?","145":"Galzus's clan, that is, the royalty of Ribaut, was destroyed in the civil war long ago by the Isaachian army led by Shannan's grandfather.","146":"Because of that, he apparently went through all manner of hardship from a young age.","147":"Such a man would hardly cooperate with Prince Shannan, his clan's enemy.","148":"I see. So that is how it is...","149":"I can guess the reason he let that girl go.","150":"After all, the Brand was on that girl's back too... Heh heh heh...","151":"Sir?","152":"N-no, it's nothing. Well, never mind. Leave Galzus alone.","153":"Forget about the girl. I can't afford to lose a bodyguard like Galzus...","154":"Pitiful. Curse your own fate...","155":"Heh... At the end... I met... someone interesting..."};
